  "text": "Skip to content\nSoren Hale\n01\nWork\n02\nServices\n03\nAbout\n04\nLab\n05\nWriting\nOpen to work from November\nGet in touch\n\n// Stack\n\nSixteen tools, used on purpose. \n\nWhat I reach for, how long I have used it and how often. If a tool is not here, I will say so before I learn it on your budget.\n\nSee what I use daily\nmain\nsoren/stack\nchore(stack): drop two tools, add none\n16 tools · 4 groups\n\nHow to read the levels\n\nDaily\nOn most working days. Ask me anything.\nWeekly\nIn regular use. I ship with it without looking things up.\nComfortable\nI can deliver with it, a little slower.\n01\nLanguages\n4 tools\nTool\tYears\tLevel\tWhat I use it for\nTypeScript\t8 yr\n\tDaily\tStrict mode, no any. Types are the first draft of the docs.\nJavaScript\t8 yr\n\tDaily\tThe platform underneath everything else, and still where the bugs live.\nCSS\t8 yr\n\tDaily\tGrid, container queries and custom properties before any library.\nGLSL\t4 yr\n\tWeekly\tShaders for charts and the occasional hero that earns its place.\n02\nFrameworks\n4 tools\nTool\tYears\tLevel\tWhat I use it for\nReact\t8 yr\n\tDaily\tServer components where they help, plain state where they do not.\nNext.js\t6 yr\n\tDaily\tThe default for products that need a server and a deadline.\nAstro\t3 yr\n\tWeekly\tFor docs and content sites that should ship almost no JavaScript.\nSvelte\t2 yr\n\tComfortable\tSmall tools and prototypes; I read it more often than I write it.\n03\nTooling\n4 tools\nTool\tYears\tLevel\tWhat I use it for\nVite\t5 yr\n\tDaily\tFast feedback is a feature. Builds measured in seconds, not coffee.\nNode.js\t7 yr\n\tWeekly\tBuild scripts, small APIs and the glue between services.\nStorybook\t6 yr\n\tWeekly\tEvery component in isolation, with its states written down.\nFigma\t7 yr\n\tWeekly\tI read design files fluently and push tokens back into them.\n04\nTesting\n4 tools\nTool\tYears\tLevel\tWhat I use it for\nPlaywright\t5 yr\n\tDaily\tEnd-to-end tests on the flows that make money, on every pull request.\nVitest\t4 yr\n\tDaily\tUnit tests that run before I have switched windows.\nTesting Library\t6 yr\n\tWeekly\tTests that use the interface the way a person does.\nLighthouse CI\t5 yr\n\tWeekly\tA performance budget the build enforces, so nobody has to argue.\n\nYears are counted from the first paid project, not the first tutorial.\n\n// Start a project\n\nTell me what you are building. \n\nThree quick picks so the first reply is useful. You finish the message on the contact page.\n\n01\nWhat do you need?\n\nFrontend build\nPerformance audit\nDesign system\nTeam embed\nSomething else\n\n02\nRough budget\n\nUnder €5k\n€5–10k\n€10–25k\n€25k+\nNot sure yet\n03\nYour name or company\nbrief.ts\ndraft, not sent\nexport const brief = {\nkind: null // not picked yet,\nbudget: null // not picked yet,\nname: null // not picked yet,\n}\n\nBrief so far: nothing picked yet\n\nContinue to contact\n\nor write to hello@sorenhale.dev\n\nNothing is sent from this page. Your picks are kept in this browser tab and wait for you on the contact form.\n\nFooter\n\nFrontend developer, Oslo\n\nWrite to me\nhello@sorenhale.dev\n\nOpen to work from November\n\n// Site\n\nWork\nServices\nProcess\nReviews\nContact\n\n// About\n\nAbout\nResume\nStack\nUses\nNow\n\n// More\n\nLab\nWriting\nFAQ\nPrivacy\nTerms\nCookies\n\n// Elsewhere\n\nGitHub\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nLinkedIn\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nBluesky\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\n\nLocal time, Oslo\n--:--\n\n© 2026 Soren Hale. Written by hand in Oslo.\n\nSorenHale\n\nCreate a free website with Framer, the website builder loved by startups, designers and agencies.",
